-Stop that.

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.367
We have to talk about
"Black Adam."

00:03:42.367 --> 00:03:43.868
Gosh, I feel like we've been
talking about this

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:46.400
for a long time.
-For a long time, man.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:47.934
For years and years and years.

00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:49.133
-You were focused on this,
and you said,

00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:51.334
"This is the one I want to do.
I'm a DC fan.

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:53.601
I'm gonna -- This is the one
I'm gonna make into a --

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:55.701
-I have been a DC boy
growing up.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:58.634
And DC -- and I'm still a boy
'cause I'll never grow up.

00:03:58.634 --> 00:04:00.601
-Yeah, exactly.
Right, yeah.

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:02.934
-So, "Black Adam" was important.

00:04:02.934 --> 00:04:05.000
And this has been
a passion project of mine.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:11.100
So, just yesterday,
I got sent the original article

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.868
announcing me playing
Black Adam 15 years ago.

00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:16.934
-Is that right?
-I pushed and fought

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:19.100
so hard for this movie
to be made.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.868
And I'll give you the context
behind that is, 15 years ago,

00:04:21.868 --> 00:04:24.667
you and I both were in different
positions in our careers.

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:27.000
-Completely.
-So, when we announced

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.000
that I was gonna play
Black Adam, it was just harder

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.534
for the studio partners to look
past the Justice League.

00:04:32.534 --> 00:04:34.734
They saw Superman and Batman
and Wonder Woman

00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:36.868
and Aquaman and Flash.
And I love --

00:04:36.868 --> 00:04:39.267
I love the Justice League,
and I love Superman.

00:04:39.267 --> 00:04:42.434
But I always felt that,
you know, if you look past that,

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:46.033
there's some really cool
characters in the DC Bible,

00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:49.467
for example, like Black Adam
has all the powers of Superman.

00:04:49.467 --> 00:04:51.634
But Superman won't kill
because he has a code of honor

00:04:51.634 --> 00:04:54.133
and a code of ethics,
which we appreciate and love.

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:59.701
But Black Adam will kill you.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.701 --> 00:05:02.200
I mean, that's it.
-That's as simple as that.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.167
Black Adam will kill you.
-Boom.

00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:07.367
-But you were telling me, when
they were making the super suit

00:05:07.367 --> 00:05:08.801
for you, for Black Adam...
-Yes, yes.

00:05:08.801 --> 00:05:12.467
I mean, you -- you are The Rock.
You are Dwayne Johnson.

00:05:12.467 --> 00:05:15.734
You are just in awesome shape.
And you go, "Yeah, all right."

00:05:15.734 --> 00:05:17.300
And you got the suit,
and the first one

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:20.934
had, like, pads in it, right?
-Dude, with the muscle --

00:05:20.934 --> 00:05:25.701
with the superhero costumes,
all throughout the super--

00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:27.834
like, Marvel and DC,
they all have these

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:29.667
muscle paddings in them.
-Of course.

00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:32.467
-Which is just what you do.
So, you can imagine

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:34.734
that muscle suit,
Black Adam muscle suit,

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:37.067
with muscle padding
on top of my body.

00:05:37.067 --> 00:05:39.334
It looked like you and I
were going back to "SNL"

00:05:39.334 --> 00:05:40.734
to do a sketch.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.734 --> 00:05:43.667
It was, like, ridiculous.

00:05:43.667 --> 00:05:45.467
So, I asked them
to remove the muscle padding.

00:05:45.467 --> 00:05:46.701
And I really wanted
to work hard.

00:05:46.701 --> 00:05:48.667
I wanted to get in
the best shape of my career

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:51.734
for this because I felt like
Black Adam just commanded

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:53.067
that kind of performance.

00:05:53.067 --> 00:05:54.767
-What does it take
to get into that --

00:05:54.767 --> 00:05:55.968
'Cause you're already
in good shape.

00:05:55.968 --> 00:05:58.634
What you're eating,
how you're working out.

00:05:58.634 --> 00:06:00.667
-It was the diet.
It was the training.

00:06:00.667 --> 00:06:01.767
It was the volume
of the training.

00:06:01.767 --> 00:06:03.901
And then, also,
the challenge is,

00:06:03.901 --> 00:06:07.901
when you get to a certain point
and you peak,

00:06:07.901 --> 00:06:10.634
the challenge was I just had to
maintain it for four months,

00:06:10.634 --> 00:06:12.033
which was challenging.

00:06:12.033 --> 00:06:15.100
But here's the thing, I got
one shot with "Black Adam."

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.000
It's the most important movie
of my career,

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.400
and I pushed all chips in.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.534
I worked my ass off,
and that's what we're gonna do.

00:06:20.534 --> 00:06:24.634
-Yeah, exactly.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:24.634 --> 00:06:29.100
So, the suit is basically
just like a skin-tight --

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:32.434
-Now it's a very thin material
that is on my body.

00:06:32.434 --> 00:06:34.300
-This is how Dwayne Johnson
looks as Black Adam.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:35.868
Look at this.

00:06:35.868 --> 00:06:37.100
That's what I'm talking about.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:40.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
Dude.

00:06:40.267 --> 00:06:42.000
I mean, dude,
this is the greatest.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.000
I think this is gonna
change the game.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.767
We saw a screening
with a bunch of people,

00:06:46.767 --> 00:06:48.467
and it was unbelievable.

00:06:48.467 --> 00:06:49.968
Getting cheers
all the way throughout.

00:06:49.968 --> 00:06:51.767
There's Easter eggs.
-There's Easter eggs.

00:06:51.767 --> 00:06:54.367
-There's Easter eggs
all throughout the whole movie.

00:06:54.367 --> 00:06:56.734
-And we also wanted to build out
the DC Universe.

00:06:56.734 --> 00:06:57.868
I've been a fan of DC --

00:06:57.868 --> 00:06:59.367
Again, as a little boy,
I was a fan.

00:06:59.367 --> 00:07:02.501
I love Superman.
He was my favorite growing up.

00:07:02.501 --> 00:07:05.901
But I didn't know until I saw
my first Black Adam comic,

00:07:05.901 --> 00:07:07.400
when I saw the Black Adam comic,

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.400
he was intense,
he looked badass.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:12.100
He had brown skin.
And I thought, "Wait a second.

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:13.934
That's me.
I want to be that guy."

00:07:13.934 --> 00:07:16.200
-Yeah.
-And so, the idea was

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.067
to build out the DC Universe.

00:07:18.067 --> 00:07:21.801
So, in "Black Adam," we
introduce five new superheroes,

00:07:21.801 --> 00:07:24.067
Black Adam and the JSA.

00:07:24.067 --> 00:07:26.501
And just so you guys know, and
many of you probably do know,

00:07:26.501 --> 00:07:29.067
the JSA pre-dated
the Justice League.

00:07:29.067 --> 00:07:32.868
So, the JSA was the very first
superhero group, man,

00:07:32.868 --> 00:07:35.801
and we stand them on their feet

00:07:35.801 --> 00:07:38.534
in "Black Adam,"
and it is amazing.

00:07:38.534 --> 00:07:39.968
-It pays off.
It's so good.

00:07:39.968 --> 00:07:42.767
And then, we all stayed
to watch the credits.

00:07:42.767 --> 00:07:45.434
And you go, "Is there going to
be a post-credits scene?"

00:07:45.434 --> 00:07:47.601
And, of course,
no spoilers here.

00:07:47.601 --> 00:07:50.067
Let's just say,
something happens,

00:07:50.067 --> 00:07:51.801
and people are gonna freak out.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:51.801 --> 00:07:54.167
-That's --
-People are gonna freak out.

00:07:54.167 --> 00:07:57.467
And fans have been kind of
asking this for a long time.

00:07:57.467 --> 00:07:59.133
And I heard that you had
a lot of responsibility

00:07:59.133 --> 00:08:01.300
for making what happens happen.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:03.934
-So, when you guys see the
movie, you see "Black Adam,"

00:08:03.934 --> 00:08:06.501
what you're gonna see --
Like I said,

00:08:06.501 --> 00:08:08.200
we want to build out
the DC Universe,

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:11.834
introduce Black Adam,
introduce other characters,

00:08:11.834 --> 00:08:14.400
as well, in the JSA.
I have been saying

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:17.634
this is a new era in
the DC Universe that I love,

00:08:17.634 --> 00:08:19.701
that we love.
It's a new era.

00:08:19.701 --> 00:08:21.634
Yes, we're going to introduce
new characters.

00:08:21.634 --> 00:08:24.667
But, also, the new era means
listen to the fans.

00:08:24.667 --> 00:08:26.033
You've got to listen
to the fans.

00:08:26.033 --> 00:08:28.534
And for a very long time,
for years,

00:08:28.534 --> 00:08:32.200
you guys know,
fans have been screaming.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:36.400
They've been upset, like, "Hey!"

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:39.100
We established Black Adam
as the most powerful

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:42.400
and unstoppable force
on this planet.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:44.767
The most powerful
and unstoppable force

00:08:44.767 --> 00:08:49.434
in the entire universe has been
on the sidelines for too long.

00:08:49.434 --> 00:08:54.767
So, myself, Seven Bucks,
Danny Garcia, Hiram Garcia,

00:08:54.767 --> 00:08:56.968
we fought, and we weren't gonna
take no for an answer.

00:08:56.968 --> 00:08:59.300
We were gonna deliver it
to the fans.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:04.400
And then, at the end,
um...welcome home.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:08.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:08.601 --> 00:09:11.601
-It pays off.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:11.601 --> 00:09:13.501
I knew you were here,
and we talked about this.

00:09:13.501 --> 00:09:15.200
You know I'm a fan of Teremana.

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:16.901
Congrats on all the awards
you win for this.

00:09:16.901 --> 00:09:18.300
-Yeah, thank you man.
-I thought we would do

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:22.200
a celebratory shot
for "Black Adam."

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:24.767
This is the Añejo.
-This is the Añejo.

00:09:24.767 --> 00:09:27.300
Thank you very much,
and thank you guys, by the way.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:28.734
You have made --
There we go.

00:09:28.734 --> 00:09:29.734
♪♪

00:09:29.734 --> 00:09:30.868
You have made Teremana tequila

00:09:30.868 --> 00:09:33.033
break all records
in the spirits business.

00:09:33.033 --> 00:09:34.601
We're gonna toast "Black Adam."

00:09:34.601 --> 00:09:37.200
But I want to say, dude,
I want toast you

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.534
for years of just being
really so kind.

00:09:39.534 --> 00:09:40.934
And you've really
been the best to me,

00:09:40.934 --> 00:09:43.634
and I really appreciate it,
even at a time in my career

00:09:43.634 --> 00:09:46.567
